  "ssml": "<speak version=\"1.0\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis\" xmlns:mstts=\"https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts\" xml:lang=\"en-PH\">\n  <voice name=\"en-PH-JamesNeural\">\n    <mstts:express-as style=\"calm\">\n      <prosody rate=\"94%\" pitch=\"-1%\">\n        Watch out for Trap Number One! <break time=\"550ms\"/> Many students pick: <emphasis level=\"moderate\">finger</emphasis> is to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">hand</emphasis>, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as tree is to leaf. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Wait a second. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Why is that wrong? <break time=\"650ms\"/> <break time=\"800ms\"/> Because a <emphasis level=\"moderate\">finger</emphasis> is a small part of a <emphasis level=\"moderate\">hand</emphasis>, <break time=\"300ms\"/> so that&apos;s <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Part to Whole</emphasis>. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Starting with tree flips it backward to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Whole to Part</emphasis>!\n      </prosody>\n    </mstts:express-as>\n  </voice>\n</speak>",
